From: V-PACE <yocto@vpace>
Subject: [PATCH] ackermann_steering_controller: pass steering and traction track separately

configure_odometry() calls the single-track set_wheel_params() overload
with whichever track belongs to the non-steered (traction) axle, so every
steering-angle calculation inside SteeringOdometry ends up using the
traction axle's track instead of the steering axle's. See the companion
patch to steering_controllers_library, which splits SteeringOdometry's
internal wheel_track_ into wheel_track_ (steering) and
wheel_track_traction_ (traction) and adds a 4-arg set_wheel_params()
overload -- this patch is the one call site that needs to use it.

wheel_radius stays picked from the traction (driven) axle exactly as
before; only the track argument changes to supply both tracks, in
(steering, traction) order.

Verified against ackermann_steering_controller 2.52.1-1 (release/humble),
ros2-gbp/ros2_controllers-release @ 3d20a0f83e63ae93479fb7b3c55dfd4a1d72a409.

diff --git a/src/ackermann_steering_controller.cpp b/src/ackermann_steering_controller.cpp
--- a/src/ackermann_steering_controller.cpp
+++ b/src/ackermann_steering_controller.cpp
@@ -37,13 +37,17 @@
   const double rear_wheel_track = ackermann_params_.rear_wheel_track;
   const double wheelbase = ackermann_params_.wheelbase;

+  // The steering-axle track (kingpin spacing) and the traction-axle track (driven-wheel
+  // spacing) are generally different -- pass both to the odometry so it applies the steering
+  // track to the steer-angle geometry and the traction track to the driven-wheel differential
+  // speed, instead of a single track for both.
   if (params_.front_steering)
   {
-    odometry_.set_wheel_params(rear_wheels_radius, wheelbase, rear_wheel_track);
+    odometry_.set_wheel_params(rear_wheels_radius, wheelbase, front_wheel_track, rear_wheel_track);
   }
   else
   {
-    odometry_.set_wheel_params(front_wheels_radius, wheelbase, front_wheel_track);
+    odometry_.set_wheel_params(front_wheels_radius, wheelbase, rear_wheel_track, front_wheel_track);
   }

   odometry_.set_odometry_type(steering_odometry::ACKERMANN_CONFIG);
